WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:10.000
How big should your emergency fund be? Start with your essentials.

00:10.000 --> 00:30.000
Essentials are what you'd need to get by for a month: rent, food, phone, transportation, and anything else you can't skip. If housing or meals are prepaid, count only what you still pay.

00:30.000 --> 00:42.000
Leave out extras like streaming, eating out, and shopping.

00:42.000 --> 00:58.000
Your first goal is one month of essentials. It's a realistic place to start, and it covers many common surprises.

00:58.000 --> 01:12.000
Your next goal is three months. That covers longer gaps, like losing a job or a bigger medical bill.

01:12.000 --> 01:26.000
Some people aim for six months, especially when their income changes a lot from month to month.

01:26.000 --> 01:38.000
Dough! picks a starting goal for you, and you can change it any time. Progress matters more than perfect.

01:38.000 --> 01:45.000
Next up: where to keep it.
